\mt1 JUDGES  
\c 5  
\p
\v 30 Will they not find him dividing the spoil? he will surely \f + \fr 5:30 \fl i.e. \ft be gracious and kind in allowing the claim of each to a share. \f* be gracious to every man: \add there are\add* spoils of dyed garments for Sisara, spoils of various dyed garments, dyed embroidered garments, they \add are\add* the spoils for his neck.  
\v 31 Thus let all your enemies perish, O Lord: and they that love him shall be as the going forth of the sun in his strength.  
\v 32 And the land had rest forty years.   
